   "reason": "DATA_GAP:capex \u2014 capex missing for FY2023 and FY2024 of the last 3 under every candidate tag the engine reads, because Kimco reports its real-estate capex (tenant improvements, re-tenanting and redevelopment of operating properties) only under the extension tag in the source. The engine applies this single value to every missing period; the value used is the filed FY2024 figure, which is also the median of the three filed years. Against the true per-year figures it overstates FY2023 capex by $60.070M (true $264.395M, ~5.6% of FY2023 OCF, in the conservative direction of lowering that year's OE) and is exact for FY2024. FY2025 is not filled (a filed value exists): its $18.4M us-gaap PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment fact understates the true $347.616M improvements line, so FY2025 OE/share in the history is flattered \u2014 the median-of-3 base is not the FY2025 year under this fill, so the flattered year does not set the base. 'Acquisition of operating real estate and other related net assets' ($277.308M / $152.943M / $218.377M for FY2023/24/25, same statement) is excluded: it is property M&A, presented separately by the filer, not capex.",
